save(37,dict(paragraphs=['Jayantika is the literary name of Jayanti Panda, an Odia poet who taught political science. In a personal recollection, fellow writer Pradeep Biswal traces her teaching career from Vyasanagar College to government colleges and her retirement as a reader at JKBK College in Cuttack. Her Kabita Live biography records her continued dedication to creative writing after retirement.','“ନିରକ୍ଷରା” questions what it means to be unable to read. Its eyes understand joy, loss and tenderness beyond the reach of grammar, while an impatient world mistrusts such sensitivity. The closing uncertainty over whose heartbeat is being heard makes intimacy itself a form of understanding.'],sources=[source('Pradeep Biswal — Dash Benhur: A Dedicated Writer','https://odisha.plus/2022/09/dash-benhur-a-dedicated-writer/',['First-person acquaintance identifies Jayanti Panda as poet Jayantika and recounts political-science teaching and JKBK retirement.'])],identity_match='Unusual pen name and political-science teaching/retirement match captured biography; source explicitly connects Jayantika with Jayanti Panda.',poems_read=[dict(id=28,title='ନିରକ୍ଷରା',basis='Full Odia original read: eyes and grammar, fear of ridicule, tenderness, impatience and shared heartbeat.')],limitations=['External biography is an attributed personal recollection, not an institutional employment record.','No book count, award or specific collection added without corroboration.','Degree/rank not expanded: source says reader at retirement, captured biography says professor; new narrative uses taught political science.','Jayantika dance organization and unrelated namesakes excluded.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review; verify bibliography with poet or publisher before adding books.'))
